<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Selgovae</h1><p class="st-meta">80 CE – 400 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of the Scottish Borders recorded by Ptolemy, whose lands around the Eildon Hills were held by the Roman fort of Trimontium.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Selgovae are known from Ptolemy's 2nd-century Geography, which places them in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, usually located in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-tweed">Tweed</a> valley and the hills of the central Borders. Their name may mean 'the hunters'. They grew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> communities whose landscape contained many hillforts, including the large enclosure on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eildon-hill-north">Eildon Hill North</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>No rulers, coins or written records survive. The heavy Roman military presence around their land, especially the fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trimontium">Trimontium</a> at Newstead under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eildon-hills">Eildon Hills</a>, has led historians to suggest they were hostile to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in contrast to their neighbours the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/votadini">Votadini</a>. Their society was rural, based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and small farms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Roman control of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> ebbed and flowed between the 80s and the 2nd century, after which the region lay beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a>. The Selgovae disappear from the record, their lands later forming part of the British kingdoms of the north.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 80 CE – 400 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:61.29%;width:6.37%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>80 CE – 400 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=240&amp;focus=selgovae" aria-label="Selgovae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4646 279 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Selgovae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4966 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4966 535h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=240&amp;focus=selgovae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

